The new[ administration], elected in May, has professed its commitment to the further liberalization of trade through free trade agreements. Its eagerness to join the mega-reg[ional] TPP is palpable. "The new government is one that will keep the policy of maximizing foreign trade agreements participation,” Trade Secretary Ramon[ Lopez] said in August.
